{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/639712-cruac-cults-encountered-or-imagined","id":639712,"title":"Cruac Cults: Encountered or Imagined","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-25T19:38:25-07:00","id":639712,"title":"Cruac Cults: Encountered or Imagined","content":"So, the Circle of the Crone isn't one unified religion, but a bunch of different cults who are unified by neo pagan philosophies and ideals. That being said, what are some cults that you may have come across in Requiem? Whether they be the work of somebody else or your own imagine? The following cults are ones I've come up with. I hope you like them! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Skinless Hand:</b> Combining blood magic with necromancy, this cult attempts to attain mastery over all things flesh. Their hierarchy is symbolic in leadership and goes in order of Muscle, Sinew, Bone, then finally The Hand. The symbolism behind their hierarchy is as follows. Muscle performs the work, Sinew orchestrates the Muscle, Bone provides the structural foundation. All working together serve The Hand's will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Order of the Crustaceous Wyrm:</b> A thoroughly unhinged cult that worships a being known as the Crustaceous Wyrm, who they describe as being half crab and half dragon. The cult devoutly believes their god is absolutely perfect in every way and all other deities are but simple children by comparison. The blood they sacrifice during Cruac rituals is offered up to the Crustaceous Wyrm as payment for the power of the spell to take effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Red Wine Society:</b> Being subject to much ridicule among self respecting kindred, the Red Wine Society is a sex cult who has little interest in the political machinations of the other covenants unless they directly inconvenience them in some way. They prefer to spend their nights fornicating with ghouls and blood dolls, living out their requiem in constant debauchery. Believing that one's spiritual awareness reaches its peak during a state of euphoria, their Cruac rituals are vulgar and perverse, mixing blood sacrifices with acts of carnal lust to bring the cast into a meditative ecstasy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Disciples of the Phoenix:</b> Believing that eternal death is an illusion so long as the soul remains immortal, these pagans worship the phoenix; a fiery bird with the power to renew itself after every death. In an attempt to emulate their patron's immortality, it is said they have created a ritual that allows them to reconstitute themselves from their own ashes. The process behind this ritual is their most heavily guarded secret.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Removed the Sanguine Sisterhood, due to it not being very good. 08-26-2015, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T02:19:30-07:00","id":640004,"title":"","content":"Very interesting, I particularly like the Skinless Hand. The Sanguine Sisterhood on the other hand... I mean, I can see what you are coming from and this is the World of Darkness and vampires tend to corrupt everything thay come in contact with, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T04:15:45-07:00","id":640048,"title":"","content":"I agree with Thorbes.<br /> <br /> It'd be interesting to see them fleshed out a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T06:29:36-07:00","id":640116,"title":"","content":"Yeah, wasn't exactly happy with the Sisterhood after giving it some thought. As for the Skinless Hand and the Crustaceous Wyrm, they're actually a running joke for me. They started out as guilds on D&amp;D Online. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for fleshing them out. I might be willing to give them a more in depth explanation, once I get around to writing out the details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-26-2015, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T07:33:52-07:00","id":640168,"title":"","content":"Another one I like is the Disciples of the Phoenix, even if the ritual to resurge from your ashes is just propaganda it is still a neat rumor to have around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T13:40:48-07:00","id":640607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/639712-cruac-cults-encountered-or-imagined?p=640168#post640168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one I like is the Disciples of the Phoenix, even if the ritual to resurge from your ashes is just propaganda it is still a neat rumor to have around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The idea I had for the ritual was it lasts for 1 death, then you have to go through the process of setting it up again. So they're not indestructible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T02:25:34-07:00","id":641294,"title":"","content":"Wait, should not all Circle of Crone cults worship The Crone herself? At least in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T03:19:12-07:00","id":641318,"title":"","content":"Not really, the crones are a loosely aligned coalition of vampires of different beliefs who came together to share mystic secrets and political power whose motto is basically &quot;Do as you will shall be the whole of the law.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T08:25:21-07:00","id":641602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/639712-cruac-cults-encountered-or-imagined?p=641294#post641294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, should not all Circle of Crone cults worship The Crone herself? At least in some way?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It sounded like that was the case in 1st edition, but apparently in 2nd, they're a collection of multiple pagan cults who share a common interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T14:13:54-07:00","id":642056,"title":"","content":"My understanding was always that the Circle, at least as an organized Covenant, largely existed as a reaction to the Lancea Sanctum. In the absence of a regimented Christian order militant making their unlives difficult and necessitating cooperation for survival it is likely that the Circle would fall apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T15:12:05-07:00","id":642127,"title":"","content":"Non the less group is called &quot;Circle of <b><i>Crone&quot;</i></b> or &quot;<b>Mothers</b> Army&quot;. I can get they now more of coalition of cults, but their title point to the idea that group as a whole at least respect the Crone. I envision that when cult want to join Circle, it need to somehow incorporate Crone ( or her variant ) in to it's mythos - maybe not necessarily as driving force, but at least figure you respect. Other way they would only be random cults, without <b>any</b> common sensibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-27-2015, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T18:03:31-07:00","id":642274,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I have to agree with WrymHamster here a bit. As they were portrayed in 1st ed they were much more tied to the whole Maiden, Mother, Crone thing so it makes their name in 2nd Ed feel a bit off. <br /> <br /> To me atleast, though I vastly prefer the 2nd ed take on them as it opens the concept up greatly more than, as a former player called it, Wicca Vamps.<br /> <br /> Feels like a revised name might have been in order for the new wider concept","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T18:37:20-07:00","id":642312,"title":"","content":"Good thing there's an entire other book coming out that's going to delve into the covenants and likely explain things.<br /> <br /> But if you want the first edition explanation, it's because the Circle of the Crone is a recognized covenant that embraces a massively wide variety of beliefs. The Circle of the Crone does not worship the Crone, but covens within are considered to be Circle of the Crone due to their embracing of pagan, disorganized belief and philosophy, and the concept of creation. There are even covens oriented around male gods. But they tend to fall under the Circle of the Crone umbrella, whether they originally intended to or not.<br /> <br /> 'Not all Circle of the Crone cults see themselves as such. The label of \u201cAcolyte\u201d gets applied by outside forces almost as often as it gets adopted voluntarily. Eventually, the reputation and power of the covenant makes it useful for many cults to go ahead and accept the mantle of the Circle of the Crone, but not all such Acolyte groups in all domains begin that way.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-27-2015, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T19:06:10-07:00","id":642327,"title":"","content":"Oh I understand all that. I've been running VtR since it came out and have nearly everybook from 1st ed. And the CotC covenant book explained the idea of individual cults having their own take. <br /> <br /> But there was a heavy emphasis that these disparate cults, even those to &quot;Male Gods&quot; still united under the central Icon of the Crone.<br /> <br /> 2nd ed's write up is a superior concept in many ways, but the name feels some what unfitting to me now.<br /> <br /> Of course I'll wait (with baited breath) for Secrets of the Covenants and see if it all fits together, but at the moment it still feels a bit off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T19:09:34-07:00","id":642328,"title":"","content":"Maybe they'll link it to the Blinded Queen or another 'Crone' founder. Similar to the Carthians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T19:24:43-07:00","id":642361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/639712-cruac-cults-encountered-or-imagined?p=642127#post642127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non the less group is called &quot;Circle of <b><i>Crone&quot;</i></b> or &quot;<b>Mothers</b> Army&quot;. I can get they now more of coalition of cults, but their title point to the idea that group as a whole at least respect the Crone. I envision that when cult want to join Circle, it need to somehow incorporate Crone ( or her variant ) in to it's mythos - maybe not necessarily as driving force, but at least figure you respect. Other way they would only be random cults, without <b>any</b> common sensibility.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be honest, we don't really know much about what / who the Crone actually is. All we know about her is she was a goddess who brought beauty to the world of mortals, drank blood to increase her power and was exiled by the other gods because of it. Outside of that brief character info, details on the Crone are pretty vague. So it's understandable there could be a multiple variety of cults who view the Crone in different interpretations. And the fact they recognize the existence of other gods shows they don't believe the Crone is the only possible religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T19:33:20-07:00","id":642385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/639712-cruac-cults-encountered-or-imagined?p=642328#post642328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they'll link it to the Blinded Queen or another 'Crone' founder. Similar to the Carthians.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work for me. The &quot;Crone&quot; is more a reference to the founding Mother-Goddesses of the Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T00:04:30-07:00","id":642705,"title":"","content":"I got the impression that the 2E Circle was the narrower concept. The three page write up refers to mothers quite a bit, while I thought that 1E covenant were supposed to cover most covenant concepts. That isn' t to say that when they encounter another cult that doesn't follow a crone figure, they'll say &quot;What? You worship a man/freaky genderless butterfly/nothing at all? You're on your own.&quot; This is how I imagine their themes manifest:<br /> * Crone figures are common, but not ubiquitous.<br /> * &quot;Do what thou wilt&quot; is their shared cause. They set aside their differences by agreeing to fight for each other's freedom. That may change when one of them gains power and their outside enemies are defeated.<br /> * Most of their predecessors didn't know about Cruac two hundred years ago, but it's shared as a weapon amongst those who agree to the above cause. Some cults may reject it, but not allies who use it.<br /> * Learning through tribulation is essential to the development of Cruac and that makes it a common philosophy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/639712-cruac-cults-encountered-or-imagined?p=642328#post642328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they'll link it to the Blinded Queen or another 'Crone' founder. Similar to the Carthians.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Led by one crazed, self-proclaimed Mother-Goddess after another, the Circle of the Crone swept through the society of the dead, not so much uniting the pagan underbelly as giving them a common name and a common purpose.&quot; So there were lots of Blinded Queens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T08:45:45-07:00","id":643030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/639712-cruac-cults-encountered-or-imagined?p=642274#post642274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I have to agree with WrymHamster here a bit. As they were portrayed in 1st ed they were much more tied to the whole Maiden, Mother, Crone thing so it makes their name in 2nd Ed feel a bit off.<br /> <br /> To me atleast, though I vastly prefer the 2nd ed take on them as it opens the concept up greatly more than, as a former player called it, Wicca Vamps.<br /> <br /> Feels like a revised name might have been in order for the new wider concept</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree. Their Covenant book gave them a much wider option including Greek Mystery cults and other stranges things.<br /> Now they seem solely dianacists. I don't see my old family trad coven fitting the new model well. Maybe secret of The Covenants will change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}